CAVEATS a reader must carry out of this table
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * A grazing transit does not determine k. Along the b-vs-k valley, a
    deeper planet further off-centre fits as well as a shallower one
    nearer the middle; SPOC's own +/-0.076 on k = 0.430 is that valley,
    not a measurement error. Quote k with b, or do not quote it.
  * These errors are photometric only. They contain no dilution error,
    no limb-darkening-coefficient error (the Claret values are held
    fixed unless --free-ld), and no stellar-model error beyond the Mann
    relation scatter.
  * Nothing here measures a mass. The package's disposition is still
    'planet candidate', and only a radial-velocity follow-up moves it.
  * PDCSAP flux is already crowding-corrected by SPOC, so no dilution
    correction is applied here. If you feed this SAP flux instead, the
    depth will be too shallow and nothing in this script will notice.
  * A dash in the T23 or ingress column is not a missing number. b > 1-k
    means the transit has no flat bottom and no second contact, so both
    are undefined. SPOC's DV nonetheless prints an ingress of 1.0767 h
    for the same grazing geometry — exactly half its own T14. Read that
    as its fitter's convention, not as a measured second contact.
